    "title": "Mohawk Ambulance donates 80 stuffed toys to Albany Med - NewsBreak",
    "text": "ALBANY, N.Y. ( NEWS10 ) — Mohawk Ambulance Service donated dozens of stuffed animals to the Bernard and Millie Duker Children’s Hospital at Albany Medical Center on Wednesday. Organizers said the donation brings much needed joy to young patients and aims to make children more comfortable around first responders. “We deal with kids on a daily basis, and at that emergency time, they are scared of us, so we want to interact with them, and hopefully, break that barrier,” Anthony Bailey with Mohawk Ambulance Service said. Organizers said they distributed around 80 stuffed animals. Read the latest from NEWS10: NEWS10 is the Capital Region’s local news leader! For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to NEWS10 ABC.",
